---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/alterj07/walkpath';
---

<Base title="About" description="What WalkPath is, how it finds internships, and how to stay safe while applying." current="about">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About WalkPath</h1>
    <p>
      WalkPath is a free, open-source board of US tech internships. Once an hour it polls the public
      job-board endpoints of the applicant-tracking systems most employers use (Greenhouse, Lever,
      Ashby, Workable, SmartRecruiters and Workday), records when the employer published each role
      and when we first saw it, and publishes everything as a static site. There are no accounts, no
      payments, no resume uploads and no server of ours that holds anything about you.
    </p>

    <h2>What "posted 2 hours ago" means</h2>
    <p>
      Posted times are the employer's own publish timestamps where the job board provides one. Where it
      does not (Workday only says "Posted Today"), the time is when our crawler first saw the role,
      which is accurate to within about an hour. Hover a posted time to see both.
    </p>

    <h2>AI summaries</h2>
    <p>
      The "Smart summary" on a job page (responsibilities, qualifications, must-have skills) is
      generated by a language model from the posting text. It can be wrong or incomplete; always read
      the full posting before applying. Each summary carries the model name and generation time so a
      bad one can be traced and regenerated.
    </p>

    <h2>Staying safe</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      Legitimate employers never ask for payment, bank details, or your SSN before an offer.
      Every Apply button on this site goes straight to the employer's careers page; we never ask you
      for anything, never email you, and never message you.
    </div>
    <p>
      Think a listing is a scam, not an internship, or not a tech role?
      <a href={`${REPO}/issues/new?template=report-listing.yml`} rel="noopener">Report it</a> and a
      maintainer will review it.
    </p>

    <h2>For employers</h2>
    <p>
      We list roles by reading the same public job-board endpoints your careers page uses, with a
      visible attribution and a link to your own apply page. If you would rather not be listed, see the
      <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/opt-out.md`} rel="noopener">opt-out page</a>; removal takes
      effect within 24 hours.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      The crawler, the site and the registry of boards are all on
      <a href={REPO} rel="noopener">GitHub</a> under the MIT licence. To add a company, open an
      "Add a company" issue. The <a href="/status">status page</a> shows the last run, boards polled and
      discovery latency.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
